INENC               Input encoder
    CLK                 Clock output to slave encoder
    PROTOCOL            Type of absolute/incremental protocol
    ENCODING            Position encoding (for absolute encoders)
    CLK_SRC             Bypass/Pass Through encoder signals
    CLK_PERIOD          Clock rate
    FRAME_PERIOD        Frame rate
    BITS                Number of bits
    LSB_DISCARD         Number of LSB bits to discard
    MSB_DISCARD         Number of MSB bits to discard
    SETP                Set point
    RST_ON_Z            Zero position on Z rising edge
    A                   Quadrature A if in incremental mode
    B                   Quadrature B if in incremental mode
    Z                   Z index channel if in incremental mode
    DATA                Data input from slave encoder
    CONN                Signal detected
    HOMED               Quadrature homed status
    HEALTH              Table status
    VAL                 Current position
    DCARD_TYPE          Daughter card jumper mode

OUTENC              Output encoder
    ENABLE              Halt of falling edge, reset and enable on rising
    GENERATOR_ERROR     generate error on output
    A                   Input for A (only straight through)
    B                   Input for B (only straight through)
    Z                   Input for Z (only straight through)
    DATA                Data output to master encoder
    PROTOCOL            Type of absolute/incremental protocol
    ENCODING            Position encoding (for absolute encoders)
    BITS                Number of bits
    QPERIOD             Quadrature prescaler
    CLK                 Clock input from master encoder
    VAL                 Input for position (all other protocols)
    HEALTH              Table status
    DCARD_TYPE          Daughter card jumper mode
    QSTATE              Quadrature state

PCAP                Position capture control
    ENABLE              After arm, when high start capture, when low disarm
    GATE                After enable, only process gated values if high
    TRIG                On selected edge capture current value and gated data
    TRIG_EDGE           Which edge of capture input signal triggers capture
    SHIFT_SUM           Shift sum/samples data, use if > 2**32 samples required in sum/average
    ACTIVE              Data capture in progress
    TS_START            Timestamp of first gate high in current capture relative to enable
    TS_END              Timestamp of last gate high +1 in current capture relative to enable
    TS_TRIG             Timestamp of capture event relative to enable
    GATE_DURATION       Number of gated samples in the current capture
    BITS0               Quadrant 0 of bit_bus
    BITS1               Quadrant 1 of bit_bus
    BITS2               Quadrant 2 of bit_bus
    BITS3               Quadrant 3 of bit_bus
    HEALTH              Was last capture successful?

SYSTEM              System control FPGA
    TEMP_PSU            On-board temperature [Power Supply]
